# Foundry orchestrator sandbox

When executing the Foundry skill (`foundry` / Software Factory v2):

## Allowed

- `foundry-invoke` fences: prepend `foundry_cli` from run context (`cli resolve`, `run init`, `run context`, `flow orchestrator-packet`)
- Only argv matching `steward_allowlist.shell_argv_prefixes` from the packet
- `Task(subagent_type={task_subagent_type})` when `steward_allowlist.task_subagent_type` is set — never `generalPurpose` when a typed subagent is named
- Pass `receipt_staging_path` / `craft_staging_path` from `observability subagent launch` into the Task prompt; never write `receipts/*.json`; never invent receipt timestamps
- Read files listed in `steward_allowlist.read_paths`
- AskQuestion when `steward_allowlist.ask_question`

## Forbidden

- `Write`, `StrReplace`, `Delete` on `{app_folder}` source/tests and under `{run_dir}` except paths in `write_paths` (normally empty)
- Authoring `{run_dir}/brief.md` or `{run_dir}/execution-graph.json` (planner owns those)
- Writing or backfilling `staging/*.json` identity fields or `receipts/*.json` after worker failure
- Raw `dotnet build` / `dotnet test` in the parent shell (use foundry-invoke `build` / `test` / `build-step verify`)
- Hand-writing receipts or inventing `--to` after failed transition
- Answering grilling clarifying questions yourself then `gate resolve --source auto`

## When blocked

Run `run block` (foundry-invoke), tell the human, wait. Delegate build/test repair to the **repairer** subagent or add a graph repair work item.

## Session stop

When `session_stop_hint` is `stop_after_worker`, `stop_after_hard_gate`, or `stop_after_build_verify`: `run handoff`, `run integrity-check`, end the chat.
